{"id":"mahabharata-2-002","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":2,"title":"द्वितीयोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 2 · Krishna returns to Dvaraka","summary":{"en":"After a happy stay at Indraprastha, Krishna takes leave of Kunti, Draupadi and the Pandavas and sets out for Dvaraka in his golden chariot with the Garuda banner. The brothers follow him a long way and return reluctantly, their hearts going with him.","kn":"ಇಂದ್ರಪ್ರಸ್ಥದಲ್ಲಿ ಸಂತೋಷದಿಂದ ಇದ್ದ ಮೇಲೆ ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಕುಂತಿ, ದ್ರೌಪದಿ, ಪಾಂಡವರಿಂದ ಬೀಳ್ಕೊಂಡು ಗರುಡಧ್ವಜದ ಚಿನ್ನದ ರಥದಲ್ಲಿ ದ್ವಾರಕೆಗೆ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸಹೋದರರು ಬಹುದೂರ ಹಿಂಬಾಲಿಸಿ ಮನಸ್ಸನ್ನು ಅವನಲ್ಲೇ ಇಟ್ಟು ಅನಿಚ್ಛೆಯಿಂದ ಮರಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"इन्द्रप्रस्थ में सुखपूर्वक रहने के बाद श्रीकृष्ण कुन्ती, द्रौपदी और पाण्डवों से विदा लेकर गरुड़ध्वज वाले स्वर्ण-रथ में द्वारका के लिए चलते हैं। भाई दूर तक उनके पीछे जाते हैं और मन उन्हीं में लगाए अनिच्छा से लौटते हैं।","te":"ఇంద్రప్రస్థంలో సంతోషంగా గడిపిన తర్వాత శ్రీకృష్ణుడు కుంతి, ద్రౌపది, పాండవుల వద్ద సెలవు తీసుకొని గరుడధ్వజ స్వర్ణరథంలో ద్వారకకు బయలుదేరుతాడు. సోదరులు చాలా దూరం అనుసరించి మనసు ఆయనపైనే ఉంచి అయిష్టంగా తిరిగివస్తారు.","ta":"இந்திரப்ரஸ்தத்தில் மகிழ்வுடன் தங்கியபின் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் குந்தி, திரௌபதி, பாண்டவர்களிடம் விடைபெற்றுக் கருடக் கொடியுடைய பொன் தேரில் த்வாரகைக்குப் புறப்படுகிறார். சகோதரர்கள் நெடுந்தூரம் பின்தொடர்ந்து, மனத்தை அவரிடமே வைத்து விருப்பமின்றித் திரும்புகிறார்கள்.","ml":"ഇന്ദ്രപ്രസ്ഥത്തിലെ സന്തോഷകരമായ വാസത്തിനുശേഷം, കൃഷ്ണൻ കുന്തിയോടും ദ്രൗപദിയോടും പാണ്ഡവരോടും യാത്ര പറയുന്നു; ഗരുഡധ്വജമുള്ള സ്വർണരഥത്തിൽ അദ്ദേഹം ദ്വാരകയിലേക്ക് പുറപ്പെടുന്നു. സഹോദരന്മാർ ദൂരം വരെ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ അനുഗമിക്കുന്നു; ഹൃദയം അദ്ദേഹത്തോടൊപ്പമായതിനാൽ മനസ്സില്ലാമനസ്സോടെ അവർ മടങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.2; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"सभापर्व","titleEn":"Sabha Parva (The assembly hall)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"उषित्वा खाण्डवप्रस्थे सुखवासं जनार्दनः ।\nपार्थैः प्रीतिसमायुक्तैः पूजनार्होऽभिपूजितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After living happily at Khandavaprastha, Janardana, honored by the Pandavas with loving affection as one worthy of honor, decided to leave."}},{"n":2,"text":"गमनाय मतिं चक्रे पितुर्दर्शनलालसः ।\nधर्मराजमथामन्त्र्य पृथां च पृथुलोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Longing to see his father, the broad-eyed Krishna took leave of the king of dharma and of Pritha."}},{"n":3,"text":"ववन्दे चरणौ मूर्ध्ना जगद्वन्द्यः पितृष्वसुः ।\nस तया मूर्ध्न्युपाघ्रातः परिष्वक्तश्च केशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He, whom the world worships, bowed his head at the feet of his father's sister, and she kissed him on the head and embraced Keshava."}},{"n":4,"text":"ददर्शानन्तरं कृष्णो भगिनीं स्वां महायशाः ।\nतामुपेत्य हृषीकेशः प्रीत्या बाष्पसमन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the greatly renowned Krishna saw his own sister, and Hrishikesha went to her with tears of affection."}},{"n":5,"text":"अर्थ्यं तथ्यं हितं वाक्यं लघु युक्तमनुत्तमम् ।\nउवाच भगवान्भद्रां सुभद्रां भद्रभाषिणीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"To Subhadra, the gentle-spoken and fortunate, the lord spoke words that were meaningful, true, helpful, brief, fitting and unsurpassed."}},{"n":6,"text":"तया स्वजनगामीनि श्रावितो वचनानि सः ।\nसंपूजितश्चाप्यसकृच्छिरसा चाभिवादितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She in turn gave him messages for her kin and honored him many times, bowing her head."}},{"n":7,"text":"तामनुज्ञाप्य वार्ष्णेयः प्रतिनन्द्य च भामिनीम् ।\nददर्शानन्तरं कृष्णां धौम्यं चापि जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking leave of her and gladdening that lovely woman, the Vrishni hero Janardana then went to see Draupadi and Dhaumya."}},{"n":8,"text":"ववन्दे च यथान्यायं धौम्यं पुरुषसत्तमः ।\nद्रौपदीं सान्त्वयित्वा च आमन्त्र्य च जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best of men duly saluted Dhaumya, comforted Draupadi and took leave of her."}},{"n":9,"text":"भ्रातॄनभ्यगमद्धीमान्पार्थेन सहितो बली ।\nभ्रातृभिः पञ्चभिः कृष्णो वृतः शक्र इवामरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wise and mighty Krishna went with Partha to the brothers, and, surrounded by the five brothers, he looked like Shakra among the immortals."}},{"n":10,"text":"अर्चयामास देवांश्च द्विजांश्च यदुपुंगवः ।\nमाल्यजप्यनमस्कारैर्गन्धैरुच्चावचैरपि ।\nस कृत्वा सर्वकार्याणि प्रतस्थे तस्थुषां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bull of the Yadus honored the gods and the Brahmins with garlands, murmured prayers, salutations and perfumes of many sorts; and having done all his duties, that best of those who stand firm set out."}},{"n":11,"text":"स्वस्ति वाच्यार्हतो विप्रान्दधिपात्रफलाक्षतैः ।\nवसु प्रदाय च ततः प्रदक्षिणमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had worthy Brahmins pronounce blessings over him with bowls of curds, fruits and unbroken rice grains, gave them wealth, and then walked around them to the right."}},{"n":12,"text":"काञ्चनं रथमास्थाय तार्क्ष्यकेतनमाशुगम् ।\nगदाचक्रासिशार्ङ्गाद्यैरायुधैश्च समन्वितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He mounted a golden chariot with the Garuda banner, swift, fitted with the mace, discus, sword, bow Sharnga and other weapons."}},{"n":13,"text":"तिथावथ च नक्षत्रे मुहूर्ते च गुणान्विते ।\nप्रययौ पुण्डरीकाक्षः सैन्यसुग्रीववाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On a fitting lunar day, under a good star and at a favorable moment, the lotus-eyed one set out, his chariot drawn by the horses Shaibya and Sugriva."}},{"n":14,"text":"अन्वारुरोह चाप्येनं प्रेम्णा राजा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअपास्य चास्य यन्तारं दारुकं यन्तृसत्तमम् ।\nअभीषून्संप्रजग्राह स्वयं कुरुपतिस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Yudhishthira climbed up after him out of love; setting aside the charioteer Daruka, the best of drivers, the lord of the Kurus took the reins himself."}},{"n":15,"text":"उपारुह्यार्जुनश्चापि चामरव्यजनं सितम् ।\nरुक्मदण्डं बृहन्मूर्ध्नि दुधावाभिप्रदक्षिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna also climbed up and waved over Krishna's head, keeping to the right, a white fan with a golden handle."}},{"n":16,"text":"तथैव भीमसेनोऽपि यमाभ्यां सहितो वशी ।\nपृष्ठतोऽनुययौ कृष्णमृत्विक्पौरजनैर्वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise the self-controlled Bhimasena, with the twins, followed Krishna from behind, accompanied by the priests and the townspeople."}},{"n":17,"text":"स तथा भ्रातृभिः सार्धं केशवः परवीरहा ।\nअनुगम्यमानः शुशुभे शिष्यैरिव गुरुः प्रियैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Followed by his brothers in that way, Keshava, slayer of enemy heroes, shone like a teacher followed by his dear pupils."}},{"n":18,"text":"पार्थमामन्त्र्य गोविन्दः परिष्वज्य च पीडितम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं पूजयित्वा भीमसेनं यमौ तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Govinda took leave of Partha and embraced him tightly, honored Yudhishthira, and likewise Bhimasena and the twins."}},{"n":19,"text":"परिष्वक्तो भृशं ताभ्यां यमाभ्यामभिवादितः ।\nततस्तैः संविदं कृत्वा यथावन्मधुसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Embraced warmly by the twins and greeted by them, Madhusudana then made his farewells to them properly."}},{"n":20,"text":"निवर्तयित्वा च तदा पाण्डवान्सपदानुगान् ।\nस्वां पुरीं प्रययौ कृष्णः पुरंदर इवापरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, sending the Pandavas and their followers back, Krishna went to his own city like a second Indra."}},{"n":21,"text":"लोचनैरनुजग्मुस्ते तमा दृष्टिपथात्तदा ।\nमनोभिरनुजग्मुस्ते कृष्णं प्रीतिसमन्वयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They followed him with their eyes as long as he was in sight, and then followed him with their minds, bound by love."}},{"n":22,"text":"अतृप्तमनसामेव तेषां केशवदर्शने ।\nक्षिप्रमन्तर्दधे शौरिश्चक्षुषां प्रियदर्शनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they were still unsatisfied with seeing Keshava, Shauri, delightful to the eyes, quickly passed out of sight."}},{"n":23,"text":"अकामा इव पार्थास्ते गोविन्दगतमानसाः ।\nनिवृत्योपययुः सर्वे स्वपुरं पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nस्यन्दनेनाथ कृष्णोऽपि समये द्वारकामगात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their minds fixed on Govinda, the Pandavas, best of men, turned back and went to their city almost unwillingly; and Krishna, in his chariot, reached Dvaraka in due time."}}]}]}